  }))), "Human Response"), mdx("p", null, "Based on the foundational work the authors discussed regarding deep learning for forecasting, there are numerous hurdles that have to be overcome despite the promising results of the PatchTST model. Many of these challenges are surrounding the practicality of utilizing a transformer model for such tasks when much simpler renditions can often lead to comparable results. "), mdx("p", null, "A major area of challenge for these models that was not covered in depth by the authors is the use of these models in scenarios where the data does not inherently have a stable cyclical nature or a low amount of random noise. In the paper all models were tested on weather, utilities use, and traffic patterns which all have heavy cyclical and predictable natures and less noise than something like a time series of human behaviors. It is relatively unclear how the model would perform in scenarios where random fluctuations in the data occur on a more frequent basis."), mdx("p", null, "As mentioned, transformer models are also much more complex and computationally intensive than standard forecasting models making them prone to a host of issues. These include the possibility of overfitting to small and homogenous datasets, the additional skill level required to ensure they are being properly utilized, and the cost that is required for training and inference tasks. These aspects are more practical than scientific in nature but still affect the potential success of the approach in more novel scenarios. "), mdx("p", null, "Finally, the authors' adaptation of language model like pre-training processes displayed signs of performance improvement but not to the same extent as experienced for text based language tasks. These processes are critical for the broader success of a language based transformer model but may not produce the same leap in terms of general forecasting performance, with basic supervised learning approaches still producing impressive results. Focusing on the improvement of these concepts has substantial potential for increasing the overall performance of transformer based time series models in a broad spectrum of domains with much less available data."), mdx("br", null), mdx("br", null), mdx("h4", {
